{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Correction / re-attribution for the 858c evidence recorded on this ticket.\n\nThe 858c reversion noted here (reopened, then read back `closed` with the rescoped description\nand both comments intact) is NOT store reconvergence and is not this ticket's subsystem. It has\nbeen traced to the Jira reconciler and filed as `e6e9-ddbf-223b-4f49` (coal-semiliquid-heifer),\nlinked `discovered_from` this ticket.\n\nProof: the reverting event is a genuine inbound write, authored `reconciler` / `env_id:\nreconciler`, and it is the LATEST status event in 858c's log\n(`1786097878273766164-d80fab3f-4d15-404c-9b20-ef7ec4fbeb27-STATUS.json`). Nothing was rolled\nback — a newer overriding event was appended.\n\nThe description-survived / status-lost asymmetry that looked anomalous under a store-level\nhypothesis is exactly what the reconciler mechanism predicts. The arbitration baseline is\nadvanced from the pass-START snapshot (`reconcile.py:595` -> `_advance_baselines`,\n`:514-531`), so it lags rebar's own outbound push by one pass. A reopen is a revert to a\nprevious value, so local came back to equal the stale baseline; `_suppressed_by_inbound`\n(`outbound_field_diff.py:323-334`, status branch `:389-396`) then read that as \"local never\nchanged\", suppressed the outbound status push, and inbound mirrored Jira's stale `Done` back\nover local. The description differed from the baseline, so it was pushed normally and survived.\n\nConfirmed in the run logs: pass N (run 31168795002) `key=REB-2500 changed=[description,status]`;\nbindings.json at f0fe2ce9d4 still `baseline.status='To Do'`; pass N+1 (run 31169292024)\n`key=REB-2500 changed=[description]` followed by the inbound STATUS write.\n\nThis does not invalidate this ticket's own store-reconvergence hypothesis for any OTHER evidence\nit holds — only the 858c comment should be re-attributed."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786122421423749001,"uuid":"86bdcfab-1e41-4878-bea1-dec2550698a9"}